1. OrthoClaim
Claims recovery for private orthopaedic surgeons
Positioning
“We recover the money your practice is already owed — and only get paid when you do.”
Target
Private orthopaedic surgeons and small multi-surgeon orthopaedic practices (especially those doing a lot of implants, trauma, and private medical aid work).
Core Offer
Audit of denied pre-authorisations, short-paid modifiers, rejected implants, and unbilled follow-ups.
Lite: Pure performance (20% of recovered money only).
Higher tiers: Monthly retainer + lower percentage of recovery.
Pricing
Lite: 20% of recovery (zero risk for the practice).
Standard / Partner: R5,000–R9,000+ monthly retainer + 10–15% of recovery.
Strengths
Extremely high ticket size once you land a practice. Very clear ROI. Performance pricing removes the biggest objection. Specialist niche is defensible.
Weaknesses
Longer sales cycle. Requires strong medical billing knowledge (or a good subcontractor). Harder to close than pure CoC work.
Realistic Net Estimates (Base case)
Month 1: R8–15k
Month 6: R70–110k
Month 12: R180–260k
Month 24: R380–520k
Odds of success
High if you can get in front of 15–20 surgeons in the first 90 days. Once you land 3–4 good practices, the business becomes very sticky.
